From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:58:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bpfloader: do not reboot when bpfloader fails on a kernel
 without eBPF

Rebased from 19.1. Same one-line change, but A13 inserted a ~24-line comment
block ("How to debug bootloops caused by 'bpfloader-failed'") between
'oneshot' and the reboot_on_failure line, so the 19.1 hunk no longer matched
by context and git am --3way could not resolve it.
---
 bpfloader/bpfloader.rc | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bpfloader/bpfloader.rc b/bpfloader/bpfloader.rc
index 0d92cd8..2a0f9c2 100644
--- a/bpfloader/bpfloader.rc
+++ b/bpfloader/bpfloader.rc
@@ -81,6 +81,14 @@ service bpfloader /system/bin/bpfloader
     #    'cannot prove return value is 0 or 1' or 'unsupported / unknown operation / helper',
     #    'invalid bpf_context access', etc.
     #
-    reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed
+    # DISABLED for msm8992/ether: this kernel (3.10.108) has no eBPF at all -- no kernel/bpf
+    # directory, no BPF options in the defconfig -- so bpfloader can never succeed, and
+    # reboot_on_failure turns that into an unbreakable boot loop:
+    #     Restarting system with command 'bpfloader-failed'
+    # Without the reboot, bpfloader still fails but init carries on and the device boots.
+    # COST: eBPF-dependent networking degrades -- per-UID traffic accounting (data usage in
+    # Settings), some firewall/VPN paths. This is a stopgap to let the rest of the port be
+    # tested; the real fix is a kernel with eBPF backported.
+    # reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed
     # we're not really updatable, but want to be able to load bpf programs shipped in apexes
     updatable
